 "body": "<p>Organizations certified to ISO 9001:2015 have until 30 September 2029 to move to ISO 9001:2026. Three years sounds generous. In practice the window is shorter, because your certification body has to become accredited for the new edition first, and because the sensible moment to transition is at an audit you already have scheduled. This roadmap sets out the work in the order that causes the least disruption.</p>\n<blockquote style=\"font-size:16.5px\">This article is based on ISO's announcement and on summaries published by certification bodies. It is not a substitute for the standard. Buy a copy of ISO 9001:2026 and confirm the requirements and your transition dates with your certification body.</blockquote>\n<h2>The timeline you are working within</h2>\n<figure style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline from 16 September 2026, when ISO 9001:2026 was published, through 2027 when certification bodies become accredited, spring 2028 when new certificates are issued to the 2026 edition only, to 30 September 2029 when 2015 certificates stop being valid. Below are five steps: gap assessment, update policy and planning, training, internal audit and management review, and the transition audit.\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" viewBox=\"0 0 502.56 255.456\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-11-10T01:57:28.142950</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.11.2, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 255.456 \nL 502.56 255.456 \nL 502.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nL 0 255.456 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 33.9948 196.63992 \nL 110.106 196.63992 \nQ 115.0164 196.63992 115.0164 194.20056 \nL 115.0164 139.31496 \nQ 115.0164 136.8756 110.106 136.8756 \nL 33.9948 136.8756 \nQ 29.0844 136.8756 29.0844 139.31496 \nL 29.0844 194.20056 \nQ 29.0844 196.63992 33.9948 196.63992 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 127.2924 196.63992 \nL 203.4036 196.63992 \nQ 208.314 196.63992 208.314 194.20056 \nL 208.314 139.31496 \nQ 208.314 136.8756 203.4036 136.8756 \nL 127.2924 136.8756 \nQ 122.382 136.8756 122.382 139.31496 \nL 122.382 194.20056 \nQ 122.382 196.63992 127.2924 196.63992 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_4\">\n    <path d=\"M 220.59 196.63992 \nL 296.7012 196.63992 \nQ 301.6116 196.63992 301.6116 194.20056 \nL 301.6116 139.31496 \nQ 301.6116 136.8756 296.7012 136.8756 \nL 220.59 136.8756 \nQ 215.6796 136.8756 215.6796 139.31496 \nL 215.6796 194.20056 \nQ 215.6796 196.63992 220.59 196.63992 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_5\">\n    <path d=\"M 313.8876 196.63992 \nL 385.0884 196.63992 \nQ 389.9988 196.63992 389.9988 194.20056 \nL 389.9988 139.31496 \nQ 389.9988 136.8756 385.0884 136.8756 \nL 313.8876 136.8756 \nQ 308.9772 136.8756 308.9772 139.31496 \nL 308.9772 194.20056 \nQ 308.9772 196.63992 313.8876 196.63992 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_6\">\n    <path d=\"M 402.2748 196.63992 \nL 468.5652 196.63992 \nQ 473.4756 196.63992 473.4756 194.20056 \nL 473.4756 139.31496 \nQ 473.4756 136.8756 468.5652 136.8756 \nL 402.2748 136.8756 \nQ 397.3644 136.8756 397.3644 139.31496 \nL 397.3644 194.20056 \nQ 397.3644 196.63992 402.2748 196.63992 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e4f1d3; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_7\">\n    <path d=\"M 114.27984 166.75776 \nQ 118.6992 166.75776 121.553312 166.75776 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 117.953312 164.95776 \nL 121.553312 166.75776 \nL 117.953312 168.55776 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_8\">\n    <path d=\"M 207.57744 166.75776 \nQ 211.9968 166.75776 214.850912 166.75776 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 211.250912 164.95776 \nL 214.850912 166.75776 \nL 211.250912 168.55776 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_9\">\n    <path d=\"M 300.87504 166.75776 \nQ 305.2944 166.75776 308.148512 166.75776 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 304.548512 164.95776 \nL 308.148512 166.75776 \nL 304.548512 168.55776 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_10\">\n    <path d=\"M 389.26224 166.75776 \nQ 393.6816 166.75776 396.535712 166.75776 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 392.935712 164.95776 \nL 396.535712 166.75776 \nL 392.935712 168.55776 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #4d7f12; stroke: #4d7f12; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path d=\"M 30.312 98.45568 \nL 472.248 98.45568 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b2a5a; stroke-width: 2.2; stroke-linecap: square\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"45.0432\" y=\"76.649296\" transform=\"rotate(-0 45.0432 76.649296)\">16 Sep 2026</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_2\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(15.977638 32.023894)\">ISO 9001:2026</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(25.892247 43.329402)\">published</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_3\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"153.072\" y=\"76.649296\" transform=\"rotate(-0 153.072 76.649296)\">During 2027</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_4\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(114.691633 26.089718)\">Certification bodies</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(125.630125 38.140929)\">accredited for</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(123.045453 50.153234)\">the new edition</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_5\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"290.5632\" y=\"76.649296\" transform=\"rotate(-0 290.5632 76.649296)\">Spring 2028</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_6\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(258.538169 26.089718)\">New certificates</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(265.391505 38.102023)\">issued to the</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(256.408052 49.338797)\">2026 edition only</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_7\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"457.5168\" y=\"76.649296\" transform=\"rotate(-0 457.5168 76.649296)\">30 Sep 2029</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_8\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(424.998956 32.115324)\">2015 certificates</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.3px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(426.487769 43.280769)\">stop being valid</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_9\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(32.743572 157.28652)\">1  Read the standard</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(45.336338 168.855807)\">and run a gap</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(48.956509 181.878672)\">assessment</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_10\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(132.798484 156.583754)\">2  Update policy,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(134.396203 168.953823)\">risk and change</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(148.767984 181.355922)\">planning</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_11\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(227.463178 156.717645)\">3  Train leaders,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(225.969241 169.828916)\">staff and internal</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(242.947725 182.188735)\">auditors</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_12\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(310.880094 157.384535)\">4  Internal audit and</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(310.3125 168.953823)\">management review</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(314.909625 182.192578)\">to the new edition</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_13\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(400.841625 157.384535)\">5  Transition audit</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(417.502359 168.985854)\">with your</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(401.377828 181.430235)\">certification body</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_14\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4d7f12\" x=\"30.312\" y=\"126.123206\" transform=\"rotate(-0 30.312 126.123206)\">Your work</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_15\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.6px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"251.28\" y=\"230.870178\" transform=\"rotate(-0 251.28 230.870178)\">Aim to finish step 5 at a scheduled surveillance or recertification audit, well before the deadline.</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_11\">\n    <path d=\"M 45.0432 102.11472 \nC 46.99658 102.11472 48.870217 101.72918 50.251466 101.043012 \nC 51.632714 100.356844 52.4088 99.426069 52.4088 98.45568 \nC 52.4088 97.485291 51.632714 96.554516 50.251466 95.868348 \nC 48.870217 95.18218 46.99658 94.79664 45.0432 94.79664 \nC 43.08982 94.79664 41.216183 95.18218 39.834934 95.868348 \nC 38.453686 96.554516 37.6776 97.485291 37.6776 98.45568 \nC 37.6776 99.426069 38.453686 100.356844 39.834934 101.043012 \nC 41.216183 101.72918 43.08982 102.11472 45.0432 102.11472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #ffffff; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_12\">\n    <path d=\"M 153.072 102.11472 \nC 155.02538 102.11472 156.899017 101.72918 158.280266 101.043012 \nC 159.661514 100.356844 160.4376 99.426069 160.4376 98.45568 \nC 160.4376 97.485291 159.661514 96.554516 158.280266 95.868348 \nC 156.899017 95.18218 155.02538 94.79664 153.072 94.79664 \nC 151.11862 94.79664 149.244983 95.18218 147.863734 95.868348 \nC 146.482486 96.554516 145.7064 97.485291 145.7064 98.45568 \nC 145.7064 99.426069 146.482486 100.356844 147.863734 101.043012 \nC 149.244983 101.72918 151.11862 102.11472 153.072 102.11472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #ffffff; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_13\">\n    <path d=\"M 290.5632 102.11472 \nC 292.51658 102.11472 294.390217 101.72918 295.771466 101.043012 \nC 297.152714 100.356844 297.9288 99.426069 297.9288 98.45568 \nC 297.9288 97.485291 297.152714 96.554516 295.771466 95.868348 \nC 294.390217 95.18218 292.51658 94.79664 290.5632 94.79664 \nC 288.60982 94.79664 286.736183 95.18218 285.354934 95.868348 \nC 283.973686 96.554516 283.1976 97.485291 283.1976 98.45568 \nC 283.1976 99.426069 283.973686 100.356844 285.354934 101.043012 \nC 286.736183 101.72918 288.60982 102.11472 290.5632 102.11472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #0b6fa4; stroke: #ffffff; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_14\">\n    <path d=\"M 457.5168 102.11472 \nC 459.47018 102.11472 461.343817 101.72918 462.725066 101.043012 \nC 464.106314 100.356844 464.8824 99.426069 464.8824 98.45568 \nC 464.8824 97.485291 464.106314 96.554516 462.725066 95.868348 \nC 461.343817 95.18218 459.47018 94.79664 457.5168 94.79664 \nC 455.56342 94.79664 453.689783 95.18218 452.308534 95.868348 \nC 450.927286 96.554516 450.1512 97.485291 450.1512 98.45568 \nC 450.1512 99.426069 450.927286 100.356844 452.308534 101.043012 \nC 453.689783 101.72918 455.56342 102.11472 457.5168 102.11472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6882f9954d)\" style=\"fill: #e07a3a; stroke: #ffffff; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p6882f9954d\">\n   <rect x=\"5.76\" y=\"5.76\" width=\"491.04\" height=\"243.936\"/>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Transition milestones reported by certification bodies, with the five steps of your own work below. Confirm dates with your certification body.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Count your audits. A three-year certificate has two surveillance audits and one recertification audit. Find which of them fall between mid-2027 and mid-2029, and pick one as your transition audit. If your recertification audit falls in that period, it is usually the natural choice, since the auditor reviews the whole system anyway. Leave at least one audit cycle in reserve in case findings need to be closed.</p>\n<h2>Step 1: Read the standard and run a gap assessment</h2>\n<p>Buy the standard and read Annex A first, since it explains the intent of each clause. Then compare your system to the changed clauses. For most organizations the gap assessment takes a day or two, because the changes are limited. Our article on <a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015.html\">what changed from 2015</a> lists them.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Question</th><th>Where to look</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Does our context review say whether climate change is relevant to us?</td><td>Context and interested-parties record (4.1, 4.2)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Can each member of top management explain how they promote quality culture and ethical behaviour?</td><td>Interview them (5.1.1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Does the quality policy follow from our strategy and context?</td><td>Policy next to the strategic plan (5.2)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Do we plan actions for opportunities as well as for risks?</td><td>Risk and opportunity register (6.1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>When we change a process, do we communicate, monitor and review the change?</td><td>Two or three recent changes (6.3)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Do people know what quality culture and ethical behaviour mean here?</td><td>Induction and training records; ask a few employees (7.3)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Do our documents cite clause numbers that have moved?</td><td>Manual, procedures, audit checklists</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h2>Step 2: Update policy, risk and change planning</h2>\n<p>Close the gaps with the smallest change that works. Resist the urge to rewrite the manual.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Policy:</strong> revise it only if it does not connect to your strategy. One or two sentences usually do it.</li>\n<li><strong>Risks and opportunities:</strong> add an opportunities section to your register, with an owner and action for each entry.</li>\n<li><strong>Change planning:</strong> add three lines to your change form or procedure: who needs to be told, how the change will be monitored, and when it will be reviewed.</li>\n<li><strong>Culture and ethics:</strong> agree with top management a short description of expected conduct and how leaders will reinforce it. If you already have a code of conduct, link it to the quality system.</li>\n<li><strong>References:</strong> update clause numbers in documents and audit checklists.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Step 3: Train leaders, staff and internal auditors</h2>\n<p>Three groups need three different things. Top management needs an hour on what is now expected of them personally. All staff need a short awareness session on quality culture and ethical behaviour, recorded. Internal auditors need training on the new edition before they audit to it. The auditing guideline, ISO 19011, was itself revised in 2026, so this is a good moment to refresh auditor training more broadly; see <a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">internal audits that find real problems</a>.</p>\n<h2>Step 4: Internal audit and management review to the new edition</h2>\n<p>Your certification body will expect to see that you have audited your own system against ISO 9001:2026 and that top management has reviewed the result. Run a full internal audit to the new edition, raise and close any findings, and hold a <a href=\"post/iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful.html\">management review</a> that covers the transition explicitly. Keep the records. They are the first thing the transition auditor will ask for.</p>\n<h2>Step 5: The transition audit</h2>\n<p>Agree the date and format with your certification body early. Transition can take place at a surveillance audit, at a recertification audit, or at a separate audit. Ask whether extra audit time will be added and what it will cost. After a successful audit and closure of any findings, your certificate is reissued to ISO 9001:2026.</p>\n<h2>Checklist</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Copy of ISO 9001:2026 purchased and read.</li>\n<li>Transition audit date agreed with the certification body.</li>\n<li>Gap assessment completed and actions assigned.</li>\n<li>Context review updated, including climate change.</li>\n<li>Quality policy checked against strategy.</li>\n<li>Risk register extended to opportunities.</li>\n<li>Change planning updated.</li>\n<li>Culture and ethics expectations agreed and communicated.</li>\n<li>Top management, staff and internal auditors trained, with records.</li>\n<li>Internal audit to the 2026 edition completed and findings closed.</li>\n<li>Management review held, covering the transition.</li>\n<li>Transition audit passed and certificate reissued.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Three mistakes to avoid</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Waiting until 2029.</strong> Auditor availability tightens near a deadline, and you lose your margin to close findings.</li>\n<li><strong>Rewriting everything.</strong> Clauses 8 and 9 barely changed. A full rewrite adds cost and introduces errors.</li>\n<li><strong>Treating culture as a document.</strong> An auditor will test it by talking to people.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Want a second pair of eyes?</strong> Chmltech helps Canadian organizations build, simplify and audit quality management systems. <a href=\"../book.html\">Book a strategy call</a> or <a href=\"../contact.html\">ask a question</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.iso.org/quality-management/iso-9001-2026\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">ISO: ISO 9001:2026, what businesses need to know</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dnv.us/assurance/Management-Systems/new-iso/transition/iso-9001-revision/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DNV: ISO 9001:2026 standard revision</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dqsglobal.com/en/explore/blog/iso-9001-2026-transition\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DQS: ISO 9001:2026 is here (transition)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.sgs.com/en-gb/showcases/iso-9001-2026-key-updates-and-transition-guidance\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">SGS: ISO 9001:2026 key updates and transition guidance</a></li></ul>\n<h2>More in this series</h2><ul><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015.html\">ISO 9001:2026: what changed from 2015</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-for-small-and-mid-sized-businesses.html\">ISO 9001 for small and mid-sized businesses</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">Internal audits that find real problems</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">Risk-based thinking in practice</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-and-ai-using-ai-tools-inside-a-quality-system.html\">ISO 9001 and AI</a></li><li><a href=\"post/integrated-management-system-iso-9001-14001-45001.html\">Integrating ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful.html\">Management review that leadership finds useful</a></li></ul>",
